1 & -3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=5$, we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=-1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=5.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b+c}{a}=\\frac{-2+5}{-1}=-3.$" 13194139536053 true] [17592186381160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381161 13194139536053 true] [17592186381160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381162 13194139536053 true] [17592186381160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381163 13194139536053 true] [17592186381160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381164 13194139536053 true] [17592186381160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381165 13194139536053 true] [17592186381160 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536053 true] [17592186381160 1041 "selection" 13194139536053 true] [17592186381160 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381163 13194139536053 true] [17592186381160 1110 #uuid "087761a1-ae97-5b4f-ac6f-9085fdab03fe" 13194139536053 true] [17592186381161 1034 "3" 13194139536053 true] [17592186381161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536053 true] [17592186381161 1111 #uuid "415f088d-64ab-5f76-a080-19b87ec58628" 13194139536053 true] [17592186381162 1034 "2" 13194139536053 true] [17592186381162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536053 true] [17592186381162 1111 #uuid "18d24a77-7258-519a-9f90-cb2d76360cbe" 13194139536053 true] [17592186381163 1034 "-3" 13194139536053 true] [17592186381163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536053 true] [17592186381163 1111 #uuid "0b97157d-9a53-5403-9446-0fe33a26f80a" 13194139